#: ../../tapes/move.rst:2 f9c335a7159d4d76bc256c0cc0a15909
msgid "Moving a tape: mount, unmount, move"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/move.rst:4 c37e300e78864ea19a9154896cb505a4
msgid ""
"The robot does three things: put a cartridge in a drive, take it out "
"again, and move it between slots. Everything else is the drive's job."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/move.rst:12 301240d108734b0da0de141ebfdb6078
msgid "One page does the first two"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/move.rst:14 b411e207c6ca4dec83ca7d822ce702db
msgid ""
"**Operator → Mount / Unmount Tape**, or **The robot → Mount or unmount a "
"tape** on the library page. There used to be two pages; the drives were "
"drawn on both and clickable on neither."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/move.rst:18 eae9cb7924784a0bb71446fa0759195d
msgid "Which direction you are going depends on which drive you click:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/move.rst:24 9e17a1b484d0441484419e628d5bb6ac
msgid "Click"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/move.rst:25 77ce745e8d964109bd9a0f3046bae007
msgid "What happens"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/move.rst:26 26483af26b2747efa091bccc42fa6671
msgid "a tape, then an **empty** drive"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/move.rst:27 f7ec76de8aaf4aefb2b08964b85ef4f6
msgid "mount - the tape goes into the drive"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/move.rst:28 70f47e498dbf425b8d1b37bb1d352452
msgid "a **loaded** drive"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/move.rst:29 27845e21edb04a32aeeab8484081f54a
msgid "unmount - its cartridge goes back to a slot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/move.rst:31 ca932bda07b445228c777bfda1987815
msgid ""
"A click only ever *selects*. The preview says what will happen and the "
"button does it, both ways round."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/move.rst:35 a68a5c3d5a694b3e831e24d12d4bca4d
msgid "Mount: slot into drive"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/move.rst:37 62c01ef9b9884168a6b868d2cc81747b
msgid ""
"Pick the library, the slot and the drive. The page shows what is in each "
"slot, coloured by generation, so an LTO-7 cartridge is not mounted into a"
" drive that cannot write it by accident."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/move.rst:41 e8b62be719b34c26b3223975c1062240
msgid "Mount Tape: the slots, coloured by generation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/move.rst:50 adec5349d0064e7e818a745f47ddb8c9
msgid ""
"The drive number is the robot's, counting from 0 - the first drive in the"
" library is 0, not its drive id. ``mhvtl status library 50`` shows both."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/move.rst:53 8d2e97231bb04d7c849703a820a4e186
msgid ""
"A drive that does not load that generation refuses, which is the point. "
"``--force`` overrides it if you are testing what the refusal looks like."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/move.rst:57 3c656fc1ecb94b09b04f379f2a09ae9d
msgid "Unmount: drive back to a slot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/move.rst:59 113ebaeafd73496ab4b263218a294a99
msgid ""
"Click a loaded drive. The slot it came from is chosen for you and "
"outlined on the map; click any empty slot, or use the dropdown, to send "
"it somewhere else."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/move.rst:62 353404e9d88e46bc84da1fb48f40ce83
msgid ""
"If that original slot has since been filled there is no default, the page"
" says so, and the button waits until you choose a free one. Being told "
"\"slot 7\" and finding slot 7 occupied is worse than being told nothing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/move.rst:73 d3334390056346308555278360a5d391
msgid ""
"**A drive whose cartridge is mounted as an LTFS filesystem cannot be "
"unloaded**, from the page or the command line. It is not a warning: "
"pulling the cartridge out from under a live mount leaves ``ltfs`` holding"
" a device with no medium, and whatever was reading it gets I/O errors "
"rather than a clean end."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/move.rst:79 e227a99f566c46ca8007f8605c5c2f1f
msgid ""
"Unmount the filesystem first - the LTFS page, or ``mhvtl ltfs unmount "
"<library> <drive>`` - and then unload the tape. Such a drive is marked on"
" the map and is not offered in the list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/move.rst:83 2963aaf3146e42bb9d7f594d62d2eeff
msgid ""
"The two senses of \"mount\" are the thing to keep straight: this page "
"moves a cartridge **into** a drive, and the LTFS page opens what is "
"**in** a drive as a filesystem."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/move.rst:87 80200e6340d74f1996023a1b03e5b60d
msgid ""
"The old ``/libraries/operator/unmount/`` address still works and sends "
"you here, carrying the library with it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/move.rst:91 ee01da5b3b2141cbb86b1b84a857cf05
msgid "Move: slot to slot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/move.rst:97 edd5e9bb3e19470fa662aa21355efa5d
msgid ""
"Tidying, mostly: putting a run of tapes in order, or clearing a slot for "
"a cartridge that has to live somewhere particular."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/move.rst:101 098f744d85fb4cc09a94b09e37bfe628
msgid "Online and offline"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/move.rst:103 a93680d3d6c9480db55eaa7d960fefdb
msgid ""
"A library can be told to stop answering the robot without stopping its "
"daemons:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/move.rst:111 82f15c61e845477593c00d9e0654ee5d
msgid ""
"Offline is refused while a drive holds a tape, which is MHVTL's own rule,"
" not this console's."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/move.rst:115 b4814cabf8214d738d4329cc2b5e2751
msgid "The MAP"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/move.rst:117 47be88e6aed8421582437f2817093f2e
msgid ""
"The mail slot, where an operator at a real library puts a cartridge in "
"from outside. MHVTL emulates it, and the console can open it, close it, "
"and have the robot re-read it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/move.rst:126 7a8c0bd908334bc38a3ed99667278b6e
msgid "Seeing the whole library at once"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/move.rst:128 57f46f4e58204f0ba1b5ba5c0680f439
msgid ""
"``op layout`` draws it: every drive with what it holds, the storage slots"
" as a grid, the import/export port, and a legend of the generations this "
"library actually has."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/move.rst:145 a4fea43d62f8439587dbb4b9b78037c2
msgid ""
"Each cartridge is coloured by its generation, in the same colours the web"
" pages use - the real LTO cartridge shell colours, adjusted so that "
"generations sharing one in real life can still be told apart. ``mhvtl op "
"palette`` prints them all with their meanings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/move.rst:150 84c456ec6ff3429b8715af6ba71d4dbf
msgid ""
"Colour is never the only thing saying what a tape is: the generation is "
"always written out beside it, so a pipe, ``--no-colour``, or a terminal "
"without 256 colours loses nothing but the fill."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/move.rst:154 b1796adc59e946a9a9a935c66f27c661
msgid ""
"``--ltfs`` marks which cartridges are LTFS volumes - see "
":doc:`../using/ltfs`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/move.rst:157 c61266999d48410fa1c83ab3543d00cd
msgid "What the robot says is where"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/move.rst:176 ce165b79ce854da39d0b869297916435
msgid ""
"This is the robot's own answer, through ``mtx``. When it disagrees with "
"``mhvtl tape list``, the library was changed without being restarted - "
"the configuration says one thing and the running robot another."
msgstr ""

